# Integer8 literal below the minimum

Verifies a negated int8 literal whose unsigned part exceeds the 8-bit
range is rejected with a compile-time diagnostic through the complete CLI
pipeline, consistent with int16 and int64.

>>> source
too_small: int8 = -128
print(too_small)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `128` for type `int8`: number too large to fit in target type at Span { start: 19, end: 22 }

<<< exit
1
